  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development shall be carried out in accordance with the reports, specifications and drawings detailed Location Plan; External Signage Pack (REV C, date 18/06/2026).\r\nReason: To ensure a satisfactory standard of development and to allow the local planning authority to review any potential changes to the scheme. \r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The maximum steady brightness of the fascia sign hereby permitted is not to exceed 600 candelas per sq.m.\r\nReason: To ensure the sign does not have an adverse effect on the amenity of the area in accordance with Council policy LP9 of the Local Plan and to comply with paragraph 141 of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Condition : 3 - The illumination of the sign(s) hereby permitted shall be by static illumination only. \r\nReason: In the interest of highway safety and of the visual amenities of the locality in accordance with Council policy LP9 of the Local Plan and to comply with paragraph 141 of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Informative: No access should be created onto the TLRN as part of the construction works. All vehicles associated with the development during the works or subsequently must comply with existing on-street restrictions. If any Red Route dispensations are sought for the works, these must be agreed with the relevant TfL team in writing before the work commences.\r\n\r\nThe footway and carriageway must not be blocked during any works associated with the development. Licencing may be required for certain operations including storing materials, scaffolding, skips, hoardings etc: https://tfl.gov.uk/info-for/urban planning-and-construction/our-land-and-infrastructure/highway licences?intcmp=3496. Note that TfL licences for these types of works do not permit any commercial advertising."
